[{:db/id 17592186119842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47833d2d-e4b4-5480-a72b-ba5cccc746dd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-47833d2d-e4b4-5480-a72b-ba5cccc746dd" :question/id #uuid "47833d2d-e4b4-5480-a72b-ba5cccc746dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-71043" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-4)}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+4}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-4:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5+3t \\\\ 1+2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+4}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-4$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\\,x=-4\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1aa198ef-bba1-5d57-9850-a75e16ce7498"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1aa198ef-bba1-5d57-9850-a75e16ce7498" :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa198ef-bba1-5d57-9850-a75e16ce7498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd35653f-734b-565e-9879-e2cd580e5dfd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77cf8edb-f11a-593d-b22b-70517358473d" "answer-2bbe3ab9-a7ef-5513-96b0-4bb81eecfdf5" "answer-7287e364-e5ae-5892-9f4f-1be7926ae48e" "answer-bd35653f-734b-565e-9879-e2cd580e5dfd" "answer-58eab78c-4412-5b45-b6ad-1d2c084a66a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77cf8edb-f11a-593d-b22b-70517358473d" :answer/id #uuid "77cf8edb-f11a-593d-b22b-70517358473d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+5}{3}=\\frac{z+1}{2},\\,x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bbe3ab9-a7ef-5513-96b0-4bb81eecfdf5" :answer/id #uuid "2bbe3ab9-a7ef-5513-96b0-4bb81eecfdf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-3}{5}=z-2,\\,x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7287e364-e5ae-5892-9f4f-1be7926ae48e" :answer/id #uuid "7287e364-e5ae-5892-9f4f-1be7926ae48e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},=x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd35653f-734b-565e-9879-e2cd580e5dfd" :answer/id #uuid "bd35653f-734b-565e-9879-e2cd580e5dfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\\,x=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58eab78c-4412-5b45-b6ad-1d2c084a66a9" :answer/id #uuid "58eab78c-4412-5b45-b6ad-1d2c084a66a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4=\\frac{z-1}{2},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119828 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-61ab7a4c-ae26-516b-9967-3f8072e6be8b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-61ab7a4c-ae26-516b-9967-3f8072e6be8b" :question/id #uuid "61ab7a4c-ae26-516b-9967-3f8072e6be8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127468" :question/problem "![](images/01/01943e80947c833ef37241fb836db96afd61731b9873cd061277a7453b34f3d8.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,3,7)$ and $Q(3,-1,1).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-1,1⟩-⟨-1,3,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-58349fdc-d11c-5b54-9386-0a54b8d936ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-58349fdc-d11c-5b54-9386-0a54b8d936ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "58349fdc-d11c-5b54-9386-0a54b8d936ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e6c04908-246a-5ae0-92f2-f471b0d7a518" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3aff6a90-29cb-5fbb-a280-7d4c79fc7881" "answer-e6c04908-246a-5ae0-92f2-f471b0d7a518" "answer-6083d104-e8d5-54a9-91d4-825774ce35f9" "answer-a3f8e739-90fc-54a0-8ff2-caa9d9c9da58" "answer-34899314-00b5-5497-adbb-b71a1ac21237"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3aff6a90-29cb-5fbb-a280-7d4c79fc7881" :answer/id #uuid "3aff6a90-29cb-5fbb-a280-7d4c79fc7881" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{4}=\\frac{y+3}{4}=\\frac{z-7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6c04908-246a-5ae0-92f2-f471b0d7a518" :answer/id #uuid "e6c04908-246a-5ae0-92f2-f471b0d7a518" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6083d104-e8d5-54a9-91d4-825774ce35f9" :answer/id #uuid "6083d104-e8d5-54a9-91d4-825774ce35f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{-4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z+7}{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3f8e739-90fc-54a0-8ff2-caa9d9c9da58" :answer/id #uuid "a3f8e739-90fc-54a0-8ff2-caa9d9c9da58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{-6}=\\frac{y+3}{4}=\\frac{z-7}{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34899314-00b5-5497-adbb-b71a1ac21237" :answer/id #uuid "34899314-00b5-5497-adbb-b71a1ac21237" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/vali